==Battleground==
*2 [[Capy|Capies]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 70~76.67 seconds<sup>2,100f~2,300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Elder Sloth]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*10 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*4 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 50~56.67 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Upgrade your wallet to Lv.3, then instantly kill the first Aku Doge with two [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] hits to break its Shield and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to finish the job. Then, use that opportunity to eviscerate the first Capy with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]] while defending with 3 cheap meatshields so that she doesn't push. Afterwards, Aku Gories can be dealt with using general damage dealers like Can Can Cat and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]. None of the enemies push very hard, so you can keep this process of chipping them up until the boss's supports are no longer, and you can target Elder Sloth directly.

